  "coverage": [
    "Optional cache/cursor publication is noexcept; isolated allocator/SQLite interception injects failures after successful commits across provider saves, appends and replacements, during load publication, and through Agent; next save checked before reload; no false receipt",
    "Actual load interleaves external SQL between provider rows and token read; active session SELECT retains old rows under old token, requiring strict validation on the next save",
    "Malformed OpenAI/Anthropic tool arguments and missing names/IDs preserve ProviderError type and full HTTP body or tool-specific fallback; real curl loopback covers six malformed-tool cases, with one request each",
    "Consumer text and item callbacks retain original JSON exceptions; cancellation keeps precedence; existing optional compaction, incomplete-event and pre-observation transport retry tests retained",
    "Repair reports evicted captures and missing references consistently across modes, honors custom roots and owned/private policies, creates durable partial archives, preserves arbitrary user JSON and tool-aware metadata normalization",
    "Coherent read snapshots and staged private backups precede the final write lock; unrelated writers commit during archive reads and backup writes; successful one-retry, second invalidation, changed target rows and changed file identities covered",
    "Repair rollback and deferred commit failure remove new candidates and preserve canonical rows, existing archives and backup diagnostics; retries retain both backups; uncertainty survives fork, relocation and repeated compaction",
    "Recovery caching charges existing serialized text, including conservative whitespace charging; private restored archives are rechecked after chmod0600; 8 MiB cache behavior and fresh runtime observations retained",
    "Existing large interleaved-session persistence benchmarks serialize 2270 suffix bytes for 20 appends, read zero unchanged rows, and retain the full-cache cap; ordinary capture scans remain zero"
  ],
